Provenance of the vendored Draco sources (skew-draco-sys)
=========================================================

Upstream release
  URL      https://github.com/google/draco/archive/refs/tags/1.5.7.tar.gz
  sha256   bf6b105b79223eab2b86795363dfe5e5356050006a96521477973aba8f036fe1
  version  draco/core/draco_version.h kDracoVersion = "1.5.7"
  fetched  2026-10-22 (re-downloaded for this check; the sha256 matches the
           one recorded by the 2026-10-22 decoder investigation)
  The encoder of the experiment's .drc frames is DracoPy 2.0.0, which
  bundles Draco 1.5.7 (decoder investigation, TODO 2026-10-22).

What is vendored (vendor/draco-1.5.7/)
  LICENSE, AUTHORS, and 196 files of src/draco/: the 63 .cc files of Draco's
  own decoder-only source list (CMakeLists.txt, the Emscripten
  draco_decoder_src groups attributes, compression_attributes_dec,
  compression_attributes_pred_schemes_dec, compression_bit_coders,
  compression_decode, compression_entropy, compression_mesh_traverser,
  compression_mesh_dec, compression_options, compression_point_cloud_dec,
  core, dec_config, mesh, metadata_dec, metadata, point_cloud, points_dec;
  without the JS glue and without mesh_splitter.cc / mesh_utils.cc, which
  CMake adds only under DRACO_TRANSCODER_SUPPORTED) and the 133 headers they
  and the shim include (closure from `g++ -std=c++17 -MM`).
  Every file is byte-identical to the tarball (`cmp`, 2026-10-22). The
  same src/draco tree was also identical (`diff -rq`, 472 files) to the copy
  the decoder investigation compiled.

Not from the release
  vendor/gen/draco/draco_features.h  hand-written; the feature list CMake
                                     writes for a default non-Emscripten
                                     build (see the file's comment)
  shim/skew_draco_shim.{h,cc}        extern "C" shim (exceptions -> codes)

Build (build.rs)
  cc 1.2.40, default flags disabled, no RUSTFLAGS inheritance, exactly:
    -std=c++17 -O3 -DNDEBUG -fPIC -ffp-contract=off
  plus the three include paths, checked against an allowlist (any other
  argument fails the build); CXXFLAGS and CXXSTDLIB and their target/host
  variants are refused; the compiler identity, the argument vector, the
  digest below and the C++ runtime (compiled-against header macros and the
  shared object loaded at run time) are reported by decoder_info() for the
  L2 meta row.

